Subject: [PATCH] vendor/openvela: build Espressif board common sources

Apply to: vendor/openvela/   (patch -p1 -d <workspace>/vendor/openvela)

boards/common/src/Makefile unconditionally built the QEMU board helpers
(qemu_weakfunc.c, qemu_initialize.c), which do not exist for an Espressif
target. arch/risc-v/src/board is symlinked to this directory, so the wrong
sources were pulled into every build of the contest board.

Include the board common Make.defs and add esp_board_spiflash.c when
CONFIG_ESPRESSIF_SPIFLASH is enabled.

Verified on ESP32-P4, openvela / NuttX 13.0.0.
diff --git a/boards/common/src/Makefile b/boards/common/src/Makefile
index dcc25de..6c362cc 100644
--- a/boards/common/src/Makefile
+++ b/boards/common/src/Makefile
@@ -18,4 +18,8 @@
 #
 ############################################################################
 
-CSRCS += qemu_weakfunc.c qemu_initialize.c
+include $(BOARD_COMMON_DIR)/Make.defs
+
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_ESPRESSIF_SPIFLASH),y)
+CSRCS += esp_board_spiflash.c
+endif
